    "body": "## Summary\n`OpenCVDynamicOpenPanguVideoBackend` sizes an `np.linspace` buffer from request `num_frames`. The only existing clamp runs when `fps > 0` and `num_frames` is at least `duration * fps + 1`, so `fps=-1` or a value just under that bound allocates from the request count. Cap `num_frames` at the container frame count before that allocation.\n\n## Changes\n- `vllm/multimodal/video.py`: after the existing fps branch, set `num_frames` to `total_frames_num` when the request asks for more frames than the container has.\n- `tests/multimodal/test_video.py`: cover `fps=-1`, a count just under the fps bound, and a request that stays within the container.\n\n## Codepath coverage\n`load_bytes` always decodes through `decode_video` → `compute_frames_index_to_sample`. Chat completions, embeddings, responses, tokenize, invocations, and offline `LLM` all reach that method via `MediaConnector` / `VideoMediaIO`. The cap is on the method, so every caller is covered. This backend hardcodes the OpenCV decoder.\n\n## Duplicate-work check\nSearched open and merged PRs for `openpangu`, `num_frames`, and `vllm/multimodal/video.py`.\n- #56390 only treats `num_frames < 0` (the linspace crash). A large positive `num_frames` with `fps=-1` is unchanged.\n- #51969 clamps `num_frames` in `VideoMediaIO.merge_kwargs` against a finite engine ceiling. It does not touch this backend, and a request value still passes through when the engine ceiling is `-1`.\n- #46836, #50990, #46153, and #55582 do not add this bound.\n\n## Tests\n- `test_openpangu_num_frames_capped_without_fps_limit`\n- `test_openpangu_num_frames_just_below_fps_bound_is_capped`\n- `test_openpangu_num_frames_within_source_unchanged`\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/multimodal/test_video.py::test_openpangu_num_frames_capped_without_fps_limit tests/multimodal/test_video.py::test_openpangu_num_frames_just_below_fps_bound_is_capped tests/multimodal/test_video.py::test_openpangu_num_frames_within_source_unchanged -v\n```\n\n3 passed. Pre-commit on the two changed files passed (ruff, mypy, test tethering).\n\n## AI assistance\nThis PR was developed with AI assistance.\n\nMade with [Cursor](https://cursor.com)",
